ler    | ?           |\n| 2        | freelancer  | animation   | ?           |\n\nNow, nationalities: Nigerian and Pakistani. Each is unique.\n\nConstraint 1: Pakistani is adjacent to videographer.  \nVideographer is in position 1. Adjacent person is only position 2.  \nSo Pakistani must be in position 2.  \n→ Therefore, Position 2: Nationality = Pakistani  \n→ Then Position 1: Nationality = Nigerian\n\nLet’s fill it all in:\n\n| Position | Job         | Movie-Genre | Nationality |\n|----------|-------------|-------------|-------------|\n| 1        | videographer| thriller    | Nigerian    |\n| 2        | freelancer  | animation   | Pakistani   |\n\nNow answer the questions:\n\n1. **What is the job of the person who is Pakistani?**  \n   → Pakistani is in position 2 → Job = freelancer\n\n2. **What is the movie genre of the person who is Pakistani?**  \n   → Pakistani is in position 2 → Movie-Genre = animation\n\n3. **What movie genre does the person in position 1 watch?**  \n   → Position 1 → thriller\n\n4. **At what position is the person who is a videographer?**  \n   → Position 1\n\nSo answers in order:\n\n1. freelancer  \n2. animation  \n3. thriller  \n4. 1\n\nFinal answer format: <solution>freelancer, animation, thriller, 1</solution>\n\nFinal answer: <solution>freelancer, animation, thriller, 1</solution>", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.12692900002002716}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -0.023342810571193695}, {"token": " told", "logprob": -1.13687264919281}, {"token": " there", "logprob": -0.3163159191608429}, {"token": " are", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " two", "logprob": -0.485468327999115}, {"token": " people", "logprob": -8.34461570775602e-06}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.0026207170449197292}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0067553711123764515}, {"token": " line", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0009178477921523154}, {"token": " numbered", "logprob": -0.08290253579616547}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.05184582